            "00055136cfaa4d0ba7281e0ff0a9cadf:2:7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Address Calculation",
          "text": "A /26 prefix leaves 6 host bits, allowing for 64 total addresses in the block. This is calculated as 2 to the power of the number of host bits.",
          "source_refs": [
            "00055136cfaa4d0ba7281e0ff0a9cadf:2:1",
            "00055136cfaa4d0ba7281e0ff0a9cadf:2:2",
            "00055136cfaa4d0ba7281e0ff0a9cadf:2:7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Network Address Allocation",
          "text": "For an address like 192.168.1.70/26, the network address is 192.168.1.64, the broadcast is 192.168.1.127, and there are 62 usable host addresses (192.168.1.65 to 192.168.1.126).",
